204	  // Latency simulation wraps both directions symmetrically so `ms` reads as a
205	  // one-way delay (round-trip ≈ 2×ms), matching how a player would set it.
206	  // Jitter randomizes each message's delay (Math.random is fine here: net
207	  // tooling, never seed-determined bytes) but delivery stays FIFO — TCP never
208	  // reorders, and the seq/journal handling downstream assumes order. Each
209	  // direction drains through a queued delay line: a monotonic delivery cursor
210	  // makes deadlines non-decreasing, and ONE timer chain delivers in queue
211	  // order. A setTimeout per message would leave ordering to the timer heap's
